The function already does almost nothing, so the only safe gain is a small one. This version gives the compiler a branch hint for the common path, where `type` has already been set and is returned directly. It also loads `profile` once into a local variable. Decoded values and return values are unchanged.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    const FIT_UINT8 t = type;
    if (__builtin_expect(t != FIT_UINT8_INVALID, 1))
        return t;

    const Profile::MESG_FIELD* const* dummy = nullptr; (void)dummy;
    const auto* p = profile;
    if ((p == NULL) || (profileIndex >= p->numFields))
        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;

    return p->fields[profileIndex].type;
}
```